Plain TypeScript Node app: no framework and no HTTP server. `src/index.ts` is the entry point{{#if (hasLibrary "evlog")}}: it initializes the evlog logger for this service and logs a `startup` event{{else}}: it only prints a greeting until you add code{{/if}}. Shared logic goes in modules of its own, under `src`.

{{#if (eq pm "bun")}}`dev` runs the entry under Bun with `--hot` and `start` runs it under Bun with `NODE_ENV=production`{{else}}`dev` runs the entry on Node through `tsx watch` and `start` runs it through `tsx` with `NODE_ENV=production`{{/if}}. There is no `build` script: the TypeScript source is what runs, and `tsconfig.json` sets `noEmit`, so `tsc` only checks types.{{#if (isMono)}} The root `{{runScript "dev"}}` and `{{runScript "start"}}` run it together with the other apps.{{/if}}
